.TH "RK\-PY\-UV Reference" "" "" ""
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]uv python list\f[R]: List available and installed Python versions
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]uv python list \-\-only\-installed\f[R]: List installed Python
versions
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]uv python install <version>\f[R]: Install a Python version (e.g.,
\f[CR]uv python install 3.14\f[R])
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]uv python dir\f[R]: Print the directory uv installs Python
versions to
.SH Tools
Install command\-line programs written in Python with
\f[CR]uv tool\f[R], which gives each one its own environment (similar to
\f[CR]pipx\f[R]).
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]uv tool install <name>\f[R]: Install a tool from PyPI
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]uv tool install git+<url>\f[R]: Install a tool from a git
repository
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]uv tool list\f[R]: List installed tools and their executables
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]uv tool upgrade <name>\f[R]: Upgrade a tool
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]uv tool upgrade \-\-all\f[R]: Upgrade all tools (also picks up new
commits for tools installed from git)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]uv tool uninstall <name>\f[R]: Uninstall a tool
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]uv tool uninstall \-\-all\f[R]: Uninstall all tools
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]uvx <name>\f[R]: Run a tool without installing it (short for
\f[CR]uv tool run\f[R])
.SH \f[CR]bin\f[R]
To print the directory tool executables are installed to
(\f[CR]\(ti/.local/bin\f[R] by default):
.IP
.EX
uv tool dir \-\-bin
.EE
.PP
\f[CR]uv tool update\-shell\f[R] adds that directory to the
\f[CR]PATH\f[R] in the shell startup files.
.SH Notes
.IP \(bu 2
uv downloads the Python version a tool needs when no matching version is
installed, so it doesn\(cqt need \f[CR]pyenv\f[R] or a Homebrew Python.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(cqt use \f[CR]pip install \-\-user\f[R] with a Homebrew Python, it
refuses with an \f[CR]externally\-managed\-environment\f[R] error (PEP
668).
